{"_set_sample_rate_from_error_sampling only sets sample_rate when client_sample_rate is truthy, so a valid client_sample_rate=0.0 is ignored, making it impossible to represent 0% sampling correctly in tests": 0.7769691348075867, "is_errors_query_for_error_upsampled_projects builds cache keys using Python's hash() of project IDs, which is process-dependent and can collide across different project sets, making the cache unreliable across workers and potentially returning wrong eligibility decisions": 0.9383567571640015, "In OrganizationEventsStatsEndpoint._get_event_stats, upsampling eligibility is computed using the outer dataset variable instead of scoped_dataset, causing incorrect upsampling decisions when _get_event_stats is invoked with a different dataset (e.g., discover during dashboard split-query logic)": 0.919175386428833}